  "id": "b5062e59-9d3c-5f7c-a4b4-eebfa9e0d5de",
  "slug": "lazy-girl-marinara-recipe-11933446",
  "name": "Lazy Girl Marinara",
  "recipe_type": "side",
  "brief_description": "This lazy girl marinara is an easy, delicious budget-busting pasta sauce. The recipe includes key techniques to make the most flavorful marinara using just a few ingredients, and comes together in about 20 minutes. Once you learn this, you'll never buy pasta sauce again.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "To begin, drizzle about 1 tablespoon extra virgin olive oil into a pan over medium-low heat. Add tomato paste and cook and stir for a few minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Next, to bloom the spices, create a small space in the pan and add a tiny splash more of extra- virgin olive oil here. Then add oregano, basil, and garlic powder, and saute on direct heat for about 1 minute."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Stir crushed tomatoes into saut\u00e9ed tomato paste and spices. Add white sugar (to replicate the sweet flavor that is so often found in jarred marinara)."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Let sauce simmer over low heat for 15 to 20 minutes. This allows all the flavors to meld beautifully, giving you Rao's-quality sauce on a budget."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Meanwhile, bring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil. Cook pasta in the boiling water, stirring occasionally, until tender yet firm to the bite, 8 to 12 minutes. Reserve 1 cup pasta water; drain."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Add 1/2 cup reserved pasta water to marinara and stir together. Add the al dente pasta; stir over low heat until well mixed together. Slowly add more pasta water as needed to ensure the sauce coats the noodles. You want saucy and glossy! Plate and serve."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Optional, but delicious: Top with a scoop of whipped ricotta or freshly grated Parmesan (or both). Enjoy!"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 30,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 10,
  "rest_time_minutes": null,
  "difficulty": "medium",
